1
00:00:05,983 --> 00:00:08,383
You're a murderer.

2
00:00:09,353 --> 00:00:10,353
What?

3
00:00:13,683 --> 00:00:15,293
Hey, Baek Mi Young, get back here.

4
00:00:25,533 --> 00:00:26,533
No.

5
00:00:27,703 --> 00:00:29,673
You're worse than a murderer.

6
00:00:38,043 --> 00:00:40,013
(Complaint: Divorce, Alimony, Division Of Assets, Minor Children)

7
00:00:40,543 --> 00:00:44,913
"Assault, profanity, verbal abuse, neglect, insults,"

8
00:00:45,423 --> 00:00:46,783
"indifference toward the family,"

9
00:00:47,183 --> 00:00:48,623
"irreconcilable personality differences,"

10
00:00:49,523 --> 00:00:50,593
"and refusal of sexual relations?"

11
00:00:51,053 --> 00:00:52,723
Jeez, with all that, shouldn't you be going to jail,

12
00:00:52,723 --> 00:00:53,923
not just getting a divorce?

13
00:00:55,893 --> 00:00:59,703
I knew Mi Young would pull something like this one day.

14
00:01:00,103 --> 00:01:01,973
Putting on that innocent face in front of everyone,

15
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:03,503
and then pulling this nonsense behind our backs?

16
00:01:03,903 --> 00:01:06,873
What? Seven hundred ninety thousand as her share?

17
00:01:08,173 --> 00:01:10,243
Does she think 790,000 dollars is chump change?

18
00:01:10,773 --> 00:01:13,613
Come on, Mom. Let's hear Won Ho's side of the story first.

19
00:01:13,813 --> 00:01:15,883
Let's see if what Mi Young wrote in this is true or not.

20
00:01:16,213 --> 00:01:17,513
Of course it's not true.

21
00:01:17,713 --> 00:01:19,823
Do you really think any of what's written here makes sense?

22
00:01:19,923 --> 00:01:23,323
- No, it doesn't make sense. - Won Ho, just trust me.

23
00:01:23,693 --> 00:01:26,463
I'll get you the best lawyer there is.

24
00:01:36,603 --> 00:01:38,403
Don't make a mistake

25
00:01:38,473 --> 00:01:42,313
Find what you want to accomplish

26
00:01:42,743 --> 00:01:46,143
Be brave and be strong

27
00:01:46,243 --> 00:01:49,513
Let go of who you are today

28
00:01:49,653 --> 00:01:53,023
Up into this beautiful blue sky

29
00:01:53,083 --> 00:01:56,153
(Husband)

30
00:01:56,653 --> 00:01:58,963
- The number is unavailable... - Darn it.

31
00:01:59,063 --> 00:02:03,763
This is why I was so against you two getting married.

32
00:02:03,963 --> 00:02:05,363
Just think if you had listened to me back then.

33
00:02:05,463 --> 00:02:06,963
Why would you be going through this awful mess?

34
00:02:08,203 --> 00:02:09,573
You must be happy, Mom.

35
00:02:09,903 --> 00:02:11,533
Since everything is going just the way you wanted.

36
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,503
- What? - Didn't you see the complaint?

37
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:16,143
"Verbal abuse, neglect, insults, conflict with her mother-in-law."

38
00:02:16,443 --> 00:02:19,213
Looks like all your hard work tormenting Mi Young paid off.

39
00:02:19,313 --> 00:02:20,343
What did you say, you brat?

40
00:02:20,483 --> 00:02:22,513
This is all your fault, Mom. Because of you, now...

41
00:02:22,583 --> 00:02:23,583
The nerve of this kid.

42
00:02:23,683 --> 00:02:25,483
- Goodness. - Mom.

43
00:02:26,023 --> 00:02:27,383
Right, this is going too far, isn't it?

44
00:02:27,523 --> 00:02:29,553
Yes, Mom. That's going too far.

45
00:02:30,293 --> 00:02:31,993
I should hit you with this. Come here, you jerk.

46
00:02:32,063 --> 00:02:33,063
- My gosh. - Hey.

47
00:02:33,123 --> 00:02:34,563
- Get over here. - You're going to kill me.

48
00:02:34,623 --> 00:02:35,693
Don't you ever think of returning here.

49
00:02:35,763 --> 00:02:36,763
You brat, I ought to...

50
00:02:40,863 --> 00:02:42,473
- Two soup and rice, please. - Okay.

51
00:02:48,403 --> 00:02:49,473
You're staying the night, right?

52
00:02:50,073 --> 00:02:51,073
Yes.

53
00:02:51,773 --> 00:02:52,783
And tomorrow?

54
00:02:53,513 --> 00:02:54,743
Are you going back home tomorrow?

55
00:02:55,283 --> 00:02:57,413
I'll stay at your motel for a while.

56
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:02,653
I'll pay for it.

57
00:03:06,563 --> 00:03:07,693
Good grief...

58
00:03:10,893 --> 00:03:13,603
So, how did things get so bad between you and your wife?

59
00:03:14,833 --> 00:03:16,803
I don't know how things with Mi Young...

60
00:03:16,873 --> 00:03:18,033
got so twisted either.

61
00:03:19,403 --> 00:03:21,803
I also have no clue what she was thinking...

62
00:03:22,343 --> 00:03:23,573
when she sent that complaint.

63
00:03:23,973 --> 00:03:26,043
Come on, there must have been some warning signs before this.

64
00:03:26,943 --> 00:03:29,383
Mi Young has always been the type to hold a grudge.

65
00:03:29,453 --> 00:03:32,053
She's the type to bottle up everything that upsets her.

66
00:03:33,223 --> 00:03:35,153
And she's not the type to forgive easily,

67
00:03:35,223 --> 00:03:36,353
no matter how hard I try.

68
00:03:37,023 --> 00:03:38,553
But you still should have tried.

69
00:03:38,693 --> 00:03:40,123
When you fight, you should just say you were wrong...

70
00:03:40,193 --> 00:03:41,363
and that you'll do much better from now on.

71
00:03:41,423 --> 00:03:43,633
You should have just sucked it up and been the bigger person.

72
00:03:43,693 --> 00:03:45,063
It's so frustrating.

73
00:03:47,363 --> 00:03:50,373
I'm telling you this because I couldn't do it myself.

74
00:03:52,943 --> 00:03:54,043
But, Won Ho,

75
00:03:54,643 --> 00:03:57,713
are the things in that complaint really true?

76
00:03:58,343 --> 00:04:01,283
No. Absolutely not. How could I?

77
00:04:01,543 --> 00:04:03,283
Right. Of course not, right?

78
00:04:03,483 --> 00:04:04,813
Well, there's your answer.

79
00:04:04,883 --> 00:04:06,723
Then there's no reason to give her an easy divorce.

80
00:04:17,963 --> 00:04:19,863
The day I got divorced and came back home,

81
00:04:20,863 --> 00:04:22,973
I found Mom in the bathroom washing a blanket.

82
00:04:23,933 --> 00:04:27,503
It was boiling hot, but she had a huge pile of winter blankets,

83
00:04:27,673 --> 00:04:29,243
and she was beating them with a laundry stick.

84
00:04:30,813 --> 00:04:33,343
Then suddenly, she started hitting her own chest with that stick.

85
00:04:34,783 --> 00:04:36,653
She was crying, beating her chest with it.

86
00:04:38,723 --> 00:04:39,953
Watching her do that...

87
00:04:41,423 --> 00:04:42,423
My heart just...

88
00:04:46,823 --> 00:04:47,823
Mom.

89
00:04:48,863 --> 00:04:49,863
Mom...

90
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:53,363
Hey, why are you crying?

91
00:04:53,663 --> 00:04:55,673
You jerk. You can't do that to Mom.

92
00:05:32,103 --> 00:05:33,103
Are you happy?

93
00:05:35,303 --> 00:05:36,313
Are you?

94
00:05:38,673 --> 00:05:39,683
You...

95
00:05:41,083 --> 00:05:42,213
Are you really doing okay?

96
00:06:02,033 --> 00:06:03,033
You...

97
00:06:03,803 --> 00:06:05,603
You're worse than a murderer.

98
00:06:09,173 --> 00:06:11,643
Right, she's already cursing me out.

99
00:06:12,043 --> 00:06:13,483
The complaint is nothing compared to that.

100
00:06:22,223 --> 00:06:23,793
(Assault, Verbal Abuse, Profanity,)

101
00:06:23,853 --> 00:06:25,493
(Neglect, Insults, Conflict With In-Laws,)

102
00:06:25,563 --> 00:06:26,823
(Indifference To The Family, Loss Of Affection,)

103
00:06:26,893 --> 00:06:28,063
(Lack Of Communication, Deep Divisions,)

104
00:06:28,123 --> 00:06:29,163
(Refusal Of Sexual Relations)

105
00:06:30,293 --> 00:06:32,733
No, that's not right. Is that my fault?

106
00:06:32,803 --> 00:06:34,503
Is that my fault?

107
00:07:02,063 --> 00:07:03,633
He called me a kid.

108
00:07:03,933 --> 00:07:04,933
A kid?

109
00:07:06,603 --> 00:07:07,833
CEO Ji.

110
00:07:08,203 --> 00:07:09,233
He called me that.

111
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:12,673
- "Wait." - That kid from Milan.

112
00:07:13,743 --> 00:07:14,773
That's what he said.

113
00:07:14,943 --> 00:07:18,473
Well, from his perspective, you probably do seem like a kid.

114
00:07:19,413 --> 00:07:20,883
It's a bit hard to see you as a woman...

115
00:07:21,043 --> 00:07:22,753
Why? What's wrong with me?

116
00:07:23,913 --> 00:07:24,913
What's this?

117
00:07:25,553 --> 00:07:27,983
Don't tell me you like CEO Ji.

118
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:29,823
Well...

119
00:07:30,553 --> 00:07:32,293
It was intense when I first met him.

120
00:07:32,923 --> 00:07:34,463
He's always surprising me,

121
00:07:34,963 --> 00:07:36,333
and I wonder about him when he's not around.

122
00:07:38,293 --> 00:07:40,233
Doesn't that mean I like him?

123
00:07:40,703 --> 00:07:44,873
But still, he's CEO Baek's husband.

124
00:07:45,873 --> 00:07:46,873
Is he?

125
00:07:47,743 --> 00:07:49,043
It looks like they're about to break up.

126
00:07:50,373 --> 00:07:51,373
What?

127
00:07:51,913 --> 00:07:55,483
I overheard him talking to a friend at a bar the other day.

128
00:07:55,913 --> 00:07:59,183
He said his wife asked for a divorce.

129
00:07:59,683 --> 00:08:02,853
Then is that why Calvin did that?

130
00:08:03,823 --> 00:08:04,823
What do you mean?

131
00:08:04,893 --> 00:08:09,033
I gave CEO Baek the party invitation, remember?

132
00:08:09,833 --> 00:08:12,803
Calvin actually asked me to do that.

133
00:08:12,963 --> 00:08:15,433
- Really? - He asked me...

134
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:18,003
to make sure CEO Baek could come to the party.

135
00:08:19,073 --> 00:08:21,943
Isn't it because Calvin is interested in CEO Baek too?

136
00:08:23,173 --> 00:08:24,673
So that's what that was about.

137
00:08:25,173 --> 00:08:28,683
Anyway, even if you end up working with Calvin,

138
00:08:29,113 --> 00:08:30,753
you have to pretend you don't know anything about this.

139
00:08:31,183 --> 00:08:32,853
Why would I work with him?

140
00:08:33,653 --> 00:08:36,093
Because you got a job there, that's why.

141
00:08:36,793 --> 00:08:38,293
I asked Calvin for a favour.

142
00:08:39,123 --> 00:08:40,563
He said you should start tomorrow.

143
00:08:41,493 --> 00:08:43,493
You did? Oh, my gosh.

144
00:08:43,763 --> 00:08:47,733
- Thank you so much. - You'll scare the baby.

145
00:08:49,073 --> 00:08:50,073
Get away.

146
00:08:51,303 --> 00:08:55,473
As you know, Cheon Man Ju's wedding has been unavoidably postponed.

147
00:08:57,043 --> 00:08:58,473
I know you were all looking forward to it...

148
00:08:58,543 --> 00:08:59,583
and must be very disappointed,

149
00:08:59,783 --> 00:09:01,013
but let's look forward to the next time.

150
00:09:01,343 --> 00:09:03,553
Still, it's a good thing a life was saved.

151
00:09:04,113 --> 00:09:06,583
You did something amazing, CEO Baek.

152
00:09:07,783 --> 00:09:10,493
Well, then, shall we start the Trunk Show meeting?

153
00:09:10,953 --> 00:09:12,993
We're finally doing this after three months of preparations.

154
00:09:13,823 --> 00:09:14,863
I hope it goes well.

155
00:09:15,123 --> 00:09:16,133
Of course it will.

156
00:09:16,193 --> 00:09:18,563
The entire staff poured their souls into it.

157
00:09:19,863 --> 00:09:21,863
You two, when Bruni arrives,

158
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:24,203
please have the relevant materials ready...

159
00:09:24,203 --> 00:09:25,633
so you can answer any requests immediately.

160
00:09:26,103 --> 00:09:27,343
Vice President Kang.

161
00:09:27,573 --> 00:09:30,313
Please prepare the VIP list for the Trunk Show.

162
00:09:30,443 --> 00:09:32,073
Yes, right away.

163
00:09:33,283 --> 00:09:36,313
Director Song, please prepare sample photos of the outfits...

164
00:09:36,383 --> 00:09:37,883
for the models on the runway.

165
00:09:39,053 --> 00:09:40,583
And the backup options too, just in case.

166
00:09:41,053 --> 00:09:42,053
Okay.

167
00:09:44,353 --> 00:09:45,993
I'm suddenly nervous.

168
00:09:46,193 --> 00:09:47,593
Of course you should be nervous.

169
00:09:47,893 --> 00:09:49,793
The brand is an icon for every bride and groom,

170
00:09:49,863 --> 00:09:52,533
and we're about to meet Bruni from Bruni & Co. in the flesh.

171
00:09:52,903 --> 00:09:53,933
That's right.

172
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:57,903
For Bruni & Co. to collaborate with us...

173
00:09:58,233 --> 00:10:00,103
is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

174
00:10:00,803 --> 00:10:03,443
So I need everyone to be on their A-game.

175
00:10:04,113 --> 00:10:05,173
- Yes, of course. - Yes.

176
00:10:06,683 --> 00:10:08,983
By the way, the venue for the Trunk Show...

177
00:10:09,053 --> 00:10:10,813
hasn't been decided yet, right?

178
00:10:12,453 --> 00:10:14,553
That's something for Bruni's team to decide.

179
00:10:15,283 --> 00:10:18,893
Bruni is surprisingly picky about the venue.

180
00:10:20,093 --> 00:10:21,093
Just like someone we know.

181
00:10:23,993 --> 00:10:26,533
CEO Ji, do you have anything to add?

182
00:10:28,033 --> 00:10:30,933
Well, I doubt my opinion is really needed.

183
00:10:31,433 --> 00:10:35,073
I'm sure CEO Baek already has all the answers.

184
00:10:35,403 --> 00:10:36,813
So then, CEO Ji,

185
00:10:36,813 --> 00:10:39,883
you have no objections to my decision?

186
00:10:40,713 --> 00:10:42,183
Kim Yu Ju for the finale model.

187
00:10:43,253 --> 00:10:45,113
What? Kim Yu Ju?

188
00:10:45,613 --> 00:10:47,283
I don't care about anything else.

189
00:10:47,353 --> 00:10:49,493
Just let me have my way on that one thing.

190
00:10:53,163 --> 00:10:55,263
Well, I'll just step out then...

191
00:10:55,663 --> 00:10:57,463
I should get going too.

192
00:10:57,793 --> 00:10:58,863
Well, then...

193
00:11:00,763 --> 00:11:03,033
Did you just say Kim Yu Ju?

194
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:05,203
Why? Is there a problem?

195
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:06,843
Of course there's a problem.

196
00:11:06,943 --> 00:11:08,373
Kim Yu Ju is the one who bailed on us...

197
00:11:08,443 --> 00:11:09,913
on the day of last year's Trunk Show.

198
00:11:10,313 --> 00:11:12,643
Have you already forgotten how much trouble she caused us?

199
00:11:12,743 --> 00:11:14,713
She had unavoidable circumstances back then.

200
00:11:14,783 --> 00:11:16,213
It won't happen this year.

201
00:11:16,383 --> 00:11:17,653
Unavoidable circumstances?

202
00:11:17,983 --> 00:11:19,723
Getting wasted because her boyfriend dumped her,

203
00:11:19,783 --> 00:11:21,223
oversleeping, and then bailing on the show?

204
00:11:21,353 --> 00:11:22,693
You call that unavoidable circumstances?

205
00:11:22,753 --> 00:11:23,753
Forget it.

206
00:11:23,823 --> 00:11:25,453
The finale model has to be Yu Ju.

207
00:11:25,523 --> 00:11:28,393
If you really hate that idea, then withdraw the divorce papers.

208
00:11:31,393 --> 00:11:32,703
Are you kidding me right now?

209
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,103
Then are we really getting a divorce?

210
00:11:36,833 --> 00:11:38,603
Forget it. We'll talk later.

211
00:11:39,103 --> 00:11:40,803
My lawyer will be here soon.

212
00:11:41,273 --> 00:11:42,303
"My lawyer?"

213
00:11:42,543 --> 00:11:44,373
Why do you have a lawyer? You have a lawyer?

214
00:11:44,373 --> 00:11:45,373
Yes.

215
00:11:47,313 --> 00:11:48,543
There you are.

216
00:11:50,053 --> 00:11:51,183
From now on, CEO Baek...

217
00:11:51,613 --> 00:11:52,953
will be speaking with me.

218
00:12:00,163 --> 00:12:01,563
She really was...

219
00:12:01,923 --> 00:12:05,363
- a divorce lawyer? - I thought she looked familiar.

220
00:12:05,463 --> 00:12:07,163
She was a client who had a dress fitted at our shop.

221
00:12:07,233 --> 00:12:09,133
From the Exclusive Line, at that.

222
00:12:09,203 --> 00:12:10,603
The Exclusive Line?

223
00:12:10,803 --> 00:12:13,003
Doesn't that mean she waited a whole year for your dress?

224
00:12:13,143 --> 00:12:14,143
That's what I'm saying.

225
00:12:14,203 --> 00:12:15,673
She once said she decided to get married...

226
00:12:15,743 --> 00:12:17,413
after seeing my dress. Unbelievable.

227
00:12:18,443 --> 00:12:20,243
Anyway, your wife is really something else.

228
00:12:20,713 --> 00:12:22,853
How could she hire a client like that as her lawyer?

229
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:24,183
Hey, hold on.

230
00:12:29,083 --> 00:12:31,153
I was wondering why the complaint was written that way.

231
00:12:31,353 --> 00:12:32,523
It all makes sense now.

232
00:12:32,693 --> 00:12:33,693
(A Fierce Lawyer's Take)

233
00:12:33,763 --> 00:12:35,063
(An Easy Guide To Law From A Divorce Lawyer)

234
00:12:35,123 --> 00:12:36,393
Once she bites,

235
00:12:36,463 --> 00:12:38,063
she looks like she'll never let go.

236
00:12:40,303 --> 00:12:41,303
But what about you?

237
00:12:41,463 --> 00:12:43,933
- So what are you going to do now? - What do you mean, what am I to do?

238
00:12:44,133 --> 00:12:46,643
She's openly bringing a divorce lawyer around now.

239
00:12:47,473 --> 00:12:48,473
Are you really...

240
00:12:48,973 --> 00:12:49,973
getting a divorce?

241
00:13:03,553 --> 00:13:05,553
- Who is it? - My mom.

242
00:13:05,893 --> 00:13:07,823
She told me to come home for a bit on my lunch break.

243
00:13:08,763 --> 00:13:10,063
She said a lawyer is coming over.

244
00:13:10,793 --> 00:13:11,793
Well,

245
00:13:12,263 --> 00:13:13,803
I guess you can't just sit back and take it.

246
00:13:15,163 --> 00:13:16,403
This is so frustrating.

247
00:13:22,743 --> 00:13:24,613
To have the wedding of a lifetime,

248
00:13:25,113 --> 00:13:27,143
I chose a dress your husband designed.

249
00:13:29,043 --> 00:13:30,313
I'm divorced too, you know.

250
00:13:31,253 --> 00:13:32,313
Come to think of it,

251
00:13:32,583 --> 00:13:34,883
I also got married in a dress my husband designed.

252
00:13:38,323 --> 00:13:39,323
But...

253
00:13:39,463 --> 00:13:41,423
do you really not have an office?

254
00:13:41,763 --> 00:13:44,763
My concept is to provide a personal, mobile service.

255
00:13:45,393 --> 00:13:48,533
Still, it must be tiring to come all the way out here every time.

256
00:13:49,003 --> 00:13:50,633
It was at first,

257
00:13:51,333 --> 00:13:52,903
but now I prefer it.

258
00:13:53,443 --> 00:13:55,103
I see much more this way...

259
00:13:55,443 --> 00:13:57,043
than I would sitting in an office waiting for clients.

260
00:13:57,443 --> 00:13:59,613
I can see so much more.

261
00:14:01,613 --> 00:14:03,383
Judging by your husband's expression earlier,

262
00:14:03,813 --> 00:14:06,023
he doesn't seem ready for this yet.

263
00:14:06,323 --> 00:14:08,553
That's actually what I'm worried about.

264
00:14:09,753 --> 00:14:13,293
I even sent the complaint, but he still doesn't seem to get it.

265
00:14:14,463 --> 00:14:17,793
Right after receiving a complaint, it's common to be in denial.

266
00:14:18,363 --> 00:14:22,063
He'll hire a lawyer soon and start fighting back,

267
00:14:22,803 --> 00:14:24,103
so don't let your guard down.

268
00:14:29,713 --> 00:14:31,273
Is this a joke? She demands 790,000 dollars?

269
00:14:32,013 --> 00:14:34,443
It says here, 790,000 dollars in property division,

270
00:14:34,513 --> 00:14:35,613
plus alimony.

271
00:14:36,853 --> 00:14:39,383
This is absolutely absurd.

272
00:14:39,583 --> 00:14:41,783
- Right? - Yes, well...

273
00:14:42,023 --> 00:14:43,993
In my opinion, about...

274
00:14:44,293 --> 00:14:45,293
forty percent.

275
00:14:45,353 --> 00:14:46,363
Excuse me?

276
00:14:46,593 --> 00:14:48,263
Forty percent or half,

277
00:14:48,563 --> 00:14:49,593
isn't that pretty much the same thing?

278
00:14:49,663 --> 00:14:52,333
Mom, let's just hear the lawyer out first.

279
00:14:52,703 --> 00:14:54,233
What about alimony?

280
00:14:54,803 --> 00:14:58,273
My son didn't do anything wrong, so we don't have to pay it, do we?

281
00:14:59,443 --> 00:15:01,303
That...

282
00:15:05,043 --> 00:15:06,683
remains to be seen.

283
00:15:07,113 --> 00:15:10,383
What does that mean? What remains to be seen?

284
00:15:10,583 --> 00:15:12,453
We hired you to find that out,

285
00:15:12,553 --> 00:15:14,983
but you're being so vague.

286
00:15:15,123 --> 00:15:16,623
Mom, why are you only talking about money...

287
00:15:16,693 --> 00:15:18,153
the moment we sit down?

288
00:15:18,223 --> 00:15:20,093
Shouldn't you hear my side of the story first?

289
00:15:20,263 --> 00:15:22,023
When it comes to priorities, the money comes first.

290
00:15:22,193 --> 00:15:23,533
Isn't that why we brought him here?

291
00:15:26,703 --> 00:15:28,463
The legal fees won't be cheap, either.

292
00:15:29,603 --> 00:15:31,233
The legal fees are pretty steep, right?

293
00:15:31,473 --> 00:15:34,473
In my case, I require a 15,000-dollar retainer...

294
00:15:35,173 --> 00:15:38,373
and a ten percent success fee.

295
00:15:39,043 --> 00:15:41,043
That's the industry standard.

296
00:15:41,383 --> 00:15:43,483
Hold on, 15,000 dollars?

297
00:15:44,013 --> 00:15:47,423
They're the ones who filed suit, so why do I have to pay that?

298
00:15:49,623 --> 00:15:52,393
I'm not doing it. I won't do it.

299
00:15:52,593 --> 00:15:53,623
I'm not doing this.

300
00:15:54,323 --> 00:15:56,363
Hey, where do you think you're going?

301
00:15:56,833 --> 00:15:58,633
It was so hard to get him to come here.

302
00:15:58,893 --> 00:15:59,963
Come on, Won Ho.

303
00:15:59,963 --> 00:16:01,903
He's supposed to be a top-notch lawyer.

304
00:16:02,133 --> 00:16:04,233
Hey, let's just hear him out. Come back here.

305
00:16:04,573 --> 00:16:05,573
Mom, didn't you hear him?

306
00:16:05,573 --> 00:16:07,003
He said 15,000 dollars.

307
00:16:07,173 --> 00:16:08,973
So you'd rather save that money...

308
00:16:09,073 --> 00:16:11,913
and let that vixen take your entire, hard-earned fortune?

309
00:16:11,973 --> 00:16:13,743
Yes, I'd rather do that.

310
00:16:13,883 --> 00:16:15,183
You want me to save money on the settlement...

311
00:16:15,243 --> 00:16:16,883
by giving a lawyer I've never even met...

312
00:16:16,953 --> 00:16:18,313
fifteen thousand dollars?

313
00:16:18,383 --> 00:16:20,983
I'd rather let Baek Mi Young take everything, all right?

314
00:16:21,053 --> 00:16:22,283
This kid is unbelievable.

315
00:16:22,953 --> 00:16:24,153
Hey, Ji Won Ho, you idiot.

316
00:16:25,353 --> 00:16:27,223
My mother's just a little upset, sir.

317
00:16:27,293 --> 00:16:29,933
I'm not doing it. I'm sorry, thank you for coming. You can go.

318
00:16:30,393 --> 00:16:31,393
Hey, you little brat.

319
00:16:46,183 --> 00:16:47,813
Darn it, I'm bleeding.

320
00:16:51,353 --> 00:16:53,053
Get out!

321
00:16:53,123 --> 00:16:55,023
Go live however you want, you rotten brat. Get out.

322
00:16:55,083 --> 00:16:58,223
- Get out! - Let go of me. I'm leaving!

323
00:17:01,523 --> 00:17:03,293
- Get out. - I'm leaving.

324
00:17:03,293 --> 00:17:04,893
- Get out. - Stop hitting me.

325
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:06,903
Darn it.

326
00:17:12,503 --> 00:17:15,573
What an ordeal. A waste of time.

327
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:17,643
Where have you been?

328
00:17:21,383 --> 00:17:22,513
Do you know what time it is?

329
00:17:24,453 --> 00:17:25,513
It's 3pm. Why?

330
00:17:25,713 --> 00:17:27,553
Did you forget that Bruni is coming soon?

331
00:17:28,453 --> 00:17:29,593
Is that today?

332
00:17:31,793 --> 00:17:35,293
CEO Ji, where have you been? Your clothes are a mess.

333
00:17:35,663 --> 00:17:37,893
- You should get changed. - No, it's fine.

334
00:17:38,093 --> 00:17:39,193
They're here.

335
00:17:59,013 --> 00:18:01,783
Bruni has chosen our Calvin Hotel as the venue...

336
00:18:02,253 --> 00:18:04,253
for the upcoming Trunk Show,

337
00:18:04,693 --> 00:18:06,193
so I've come to see you all today.

338
00:18:07,023 --> 00:18:09,393
So that the collaborative show between J&White and Bruni...

339
00:18:09,593 --> 00:18:11,763
can proceed without any problems,

340
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:13,703
I will do my absolute best.

341
00:18:15,633 --> 00:18:17,803
Yes. I hope everyone does their best on this Trunk Show...

342
00:18:17,933 --> 00:18:20,343
so we can achieve the best possible results.

343
00:18:24,443 --> 00:18:25,513
CEO Baek?

344
00:18:26,283 --> 00:18:27,283
Yes?

345
00:18:28,413 --> 00:18:30,753
Yes. We at J&White...

346
00:18:31,213 --> 00:18:34,123
will prepare the most exquisite dresses...

347
00:18:34,723 --> 00:18:36,693
that will best accentuate Bruni's jewellery.

348
00:18:37,393 --> 00:18:41,263
Then I suppose it's my job to find a Cinderella worthy of them.

349
00:18:42,323 --> 00:18:43,363
Well,

350
00:18:43,363 --> 00:18:45,233
I have one other task I'm in charge of.

351
00:18:45,763 --> 00:18:47,903
The model for the finale...

352
00:18:48,263 --> 00:18:50,203
is my responsibility to cast.

353
00:18:53,073 --> 00:18:55,403
For someone in the hotel business, Calvin,

354
00:18:56,003 --> 00:18:57,613
you certainly have your hands in a lot of things.

355
00:18:57,843 --> 00:19:00,083
I'm known for being well-connected in this field,

356
00:19:00,613 --> 00:19:02,313
so you can trust me with this.

357
00:19:03,383 --> 00:19:05,113
I'm afraid that will be a problem.

358
00:19:05,953 --> 00:19:09,223
As for the model for the finale, we've already completed the casting.

359
00:19:10,793 --> 00:19:12,053
You already did? When?

360
00:19:14,723 --> 00:19:15,863
Won Ho, what are you doing?

361
00:19:16,763 --> 00:19:19,633
Have you already forgotten we chose a model?

362
00:19:21,403 --> 00:19:23,033
The model for the finale of this show...

363
00:19:23,473 --> 00:19:25,003
will be Kim Yu Ju.

364
00:19:25,833 --> 00:19:28,243
Ms. Kim is a long time muse...

365
00:19:28,543 --> 00:19:31,243
who provides my husband with design inspiration.

366
00:19:31,613 --> 00:19:34,643
So, Kim Yu Ju is your husband's muse.

367
00:19:37,453 --> 00:19:38,753
Then let's proceed with that.

368
00:19:50,263 --> 00:19:51,663
"There is no way I'm working with Kim Yu Ju."

369
00:19:51,733 --> 00:19:53,003
"Absolutely not to Kim Yu Ju."

370
00:19:53,063 --> 00:19:54,863
And now, all of a sudden, she's my "muse?"

371
00:19:55,063 --> 00:19:56,433
Did you eat something bad for lunch?

372
00:19:56,603 --> 00:19:57,773
You're the one who said...

373
00:19:58,103 --> 00:20:01,173
it had to be Kim Yu Ju. That if I didn't use Kim Yu Ju,

374
00:20:01,243 --> 00:20:02,373
I should withdraw the complaint.

375
00:20:03,113 --> 00:20:04,173
Wait, don't tell me...

376
00:20:04,973 --> 00:20:06,913
you only agreed to use Kim Yu Ju because of that?

377
00:20:07,343 --> 00:20:08,343
Of course.

378
00:20:09,113 --> 00:20:10,613
Right. Of course.

379
00:20:11,683 --> 00:20:14,583
But how can you act so natural about it?

380
00:20:15,053 --> 00:20:17,193
- About what? - You and Calvin.

381
00:20:17,923 --> 00:20:19,763
As if nothing ever happened between you two.

382
00:20:20,023 --> 00:20:21,893
What are you trying to say?

383
00:20:22,393 --> 00:20:24,493
A normal person would feel a little...

384
00:20:24,733 --> 00:20:27,603
uncomfortable and upset. Wouldn't you agree?

385
00:20:28,063 --> 00:20:31,833
How can you smile so naturally? It's unbelievable.

386
00:20:32,003 --> 00:20:33,203
Smile? Who was smiling?

387
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:35,743
Who was smiling? I saw you give him a huge smile.

388
00:20:36,103 --> 00:20:38,573
This is your problem.

389
00:20:38,643 --> 00:20:40,183
What's my problem now?

390
00:20:40,283 --> 00:20:43,283
Calvin managed to win over Bruni and is expanding his business,

391
00:20:43,413 --> 00:20:45,153
while you're here thinking such pathetic things.

392
00:20:45,913 --> 00:20:48,023
What? Are you comparing me to Calvin right now?

393
00:20:48,453 --> 00:20:50,053
Are you embarrassed by me? Is that it?

394
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:51,153
I am embarrassed.

395
00:20:51,653 --> 00:20:52,793
Just look at yourself.

396
00:20:52,853 --> 00:20:54,493
What do you think Calvin thinks of you?

397
00:20:54,763 --> 00:20:56,893
You couldn't even help me save face in front of my ex.

398
00:20:56,963 --> 00:20:58,433
The fact that you're my husband...

399
00:20:58,793 --> 00:21:00,863
is so embarrassing. Happy now?

400
00:21:15,083 --> 00:21:17,213
Isn't Calvin drop-dead gorgeous in person?

401
00:21:17,383 --> 00:21:19,153
I know. He's handsome,

402
00:21:19,153 --> 00:21:20,323
and they say he's super talented too.

403
00:21:20,723 --> 00:21:22,183
The Trunk Show is going to be amazing, right?

404
00:21:22,453 --> 00:21:24,553
- Yes. - Of course. It's his hotel.

405
00:21:24,623 --> 00:21:27,393
- That's true. - I'm excited thinking about it.

406
00:21:27,463 --> 00:21:29,663
Stop chitchatting and let's focus.

407
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:30,733
- Okay. - Okay.

408
00:21:57,553 --> 00:21:58,823
I told you not to come back.

409
00:21:59,493 --> 00:22:02,063
Why are you suddenly treating me like this?

410
00:22:02,363 --> 00:22:05,663
- Don't do this to me. - I told you, I'm getting married.

411
00:22:08,033 --> 00:22:09,973
I don't want to make you feel any more miserable.

412
00:22:34,063 --> 00:22:35,163
Look,

413
00:22:36,023 --> 00:22:38,093
from now on, just pretend you don't know me.

414
00:22:39,293 --> 00:22:40,333
To me,

415
00:22:41,003 --> 00:22:43,373
you are like someone who doesn't exist.

416
00:22:59,613 --> 00:23:02,053
- Yes? - You have a visitor.

417
00:23:02,883 --> 00:23:05,323
- Who is it? - It's Ms. Baek Mi Young.

418
00:23:06,123 --> 00:23:07,223
Show her in.

419
00:23:12,793 --> 00:23:14,903
What brings you here? Have a seat.

420
00:23:15,803 --> 00:23:17,073
Was this part of your plan too?

421
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:20,303
- What? - The fact that Bruni chose...

422
00:23:20,373 --> 00:23:21,673
the Calvin Hotel for the Trunk Show.

423
00:23:23,003 --> 00:23:24,143
That wasn't a coincidence, was it?

424
00:23:24,573 --> 00:23:26,143
I made a strong pitch for it.

425
00:23:27,243 --> 00:23:28,943
I knew you were collaborating with Bruni.

426
00:23:30,953 --> 00:23:31,953
Why?

427
00:23:32,583 --> 00:23:33,753
Because you wanted to see me again?

428
00:23:36,923 --> 00:23:38,523
Fine. It doesn't matter.

429
00:23:39,123 --> 00:23:41,023
No matter what you're plotting,

430
00:23:41,593 --> 00:23:43,433
I won't even bat an eye.

431
00:23:44,663 --> 00:23:45,663
But...

432
00:23:46,433 --> 00:23:48,003
please don't cross the line.

433
00:23:49,263 --> 00:23:52,073
The moment you cross that line, be it in business or anything else,

434
00:23:53,573 --> 00:23:55,143
I won't just stand by.

435
00:24:26,033 --> 00:24:27,343
Are you embarrassed by me?

436
00:24:27,643 --> 00:24:29,473
I am embarrassed.

437
00:24:29,703 --> 00:24:31,943
You couldn't even help me save face in front of my ex.

438
00:24:32,013 --> 00:24:33,883
The fact that you're my husband...

439
00:24:34,043 --> 00:24:35,443
is so embarrassing.

440
00:24:57,803 --> 00:25:00,443
I think my wife really hates me.

441
00:25:01,003 --> 00:25:03,043
If she liked you, would she be asking for a divorce?

442
00:25:04,073 --> 00:25:05,173
What the heck?

443
00:25:05,873 --> 00:25:07,843
Why are you so blunt, Father?

444
00:25:08,243 --> 00:25:10,683
If you're looking for comfort, you should pray.

445
00:25:11,213 --> 00:25:13,523
Find your peace with the Lord.

446
00:25:17,723 --> 00:25:19,053
About that day...

447
00:25:19,253 --> 00:25:21,893
Have you thought about being honest with your wife about it?

448
00:25:23,193 --> 00:25:25,533
- That day? - You know.

449
00:25:26,093 --> 00:25:27,233
Three years ago.

450
00:25:31,503 --> 00:25:34,803
Mi Young, just put that down. Okay? Put it down right now.

451
00:25:34,873 --> 00:25:37,973
- Stop. Don't come any closer. - Put it down.

452
00:25:38,843 --> 00:25:39,843
Darn it.

453
00:25:42,043 --> 00:25:43,083
Stop.

454
00:25:43,353 --> 00:25:44,453
Darn it.

455
00:25:46,283 --> 00:25:47,823
The way you two ended up...

456
00:25:47,883 --> 00:25:49,553
I wonder if it's because of that.

457
00:25:50,523 --> 00:25:52,123
And if I think about it more,

458
00:25:52,423 --> 00:25:54,163
I start to wonder if it's my fault.

459
00:25:55,123 --> 00:25:58,193
Come on, that's not why. It's not your fault, Father.

460
00:25:58,733 --> 00:25:59,963
Don't think like that.

461
00:26:10,743 --> 00:26:15,183
Prayers are for the Lord, and counselling is for professionals.

462
00:26:23,083 --> 00:26:25,793
(Bae Su Ji, Lawyer, Neighbourhood Law Office)

463
00:26:25,893 --> 00:26:29,523
(Bae Su Ji Law Office)

464
00:26:55,553 --> 00:26:56,723
Excuse me.

465
00:26:59,393 --> 00:27:00,393
Yes?

466
00:27:00,723 --> 00:27:05,093
Hello. I was referred here.

467
00:27:05,263 --> 00:27:06,263
Well...

468
00:27:08,933 --> 00:27:12,573
I'd like to get some advice about a divorce.

469
00:27:12,973 --> 00:27:14,473
You're in the right place.

470
00:27:14,703 --> 00:27:17,643
This firm's been the go-to spot for 30 years.

471
00:27:18,013 --> 00:27:19,473
Thirty years?

472
00:27:20,143 --> 00:27:22,513
So, when did you start working here...

473
00:27:22,583 --> 00:27:24,683
And why are you asking?

474
00:27:25,913 --> 00:27:27,423
What is this, an interrogation?

475
00:27:46,873 --> 00:27:49,573
I like my meat well-done. Is that okay with you?

476
00:27:49,643 --> 00:27:50,773
Yes, of course.

477
00:27:52,673 --> 00:27:53,743
By the way,

478
00:27:54,113 --> 00:27:56,243
is that your real name?

479
00:27:57,783 --> 00:27:58,853
No, it's just...

480
00:27:58,913 --> 00:28:00,423
It's just that when I first heard your name,

481
00:28:00,423 --> 00:28:02,383
I thought you were a young woman.

482
00:28:08,023 --> 00:28:09,523
I used to be a woman.

483
00:28:09,923 --> 00:28:10,933
What?

484
00:28:11,893 --> 00:28:13,063
In my past life.

485
00:28:13,333 --> 00:28:15,333
In your past life...

486
00:28:19,973 --> 00:28:21,303
Father Kwon sent you?

487
00:28:21,743 --> 00:28:24,213
Yes. He said...

488
00:28:24,273 --> 00:28:26,713
you're an expert in divorce cases.

489
00:28:27,713 --> 00:28:28,843
An expert?

490
00:28:35,953 --> 00:28:38,093
I'm a heavyweight in this business.

491
00:28:39,393 --> 00:28:42,363
So, in your past life, you were a woman,

492
00:28:42,363 --> 00:28:44,963
and in this life, you're a heavyweight?

493
00:28:47,433 --> 00:28:48,433
I see.

494
00:28:49,803 --> 00:28:51,333
If you got served anything, let me see it.

495
00:28:53,073 --> 00:28:55,943
- The complaint you were served. - Yes.

496
00:28:59,443 --> 00:29:00,643
(Yeonnam Family Court)

497
00:29:15,393 --> 00:29:16,763
Let's see.

498
00:29:21,633 --> 00:29:23,573
The grounds for divorce are...

499
00:29:24,673 --> 00:29:28,073
- Verbal abuse, assault, contempt... - Excuse me, sir.

500
00:29:28,473 --> 00:29:30,103
Could you please keep your voice down?

501
00:29:31,813 --> 00:29:33,543
So you have the decency to be embarrassed.

502
00:29:35,383 --> 00:29:36,843
Seven hundred ninety thousand is a bargain.

503
00:29:37,853 --> 00:29:38,853
What?

504
00:29:39,083 --> 00:29:41,423
If all this is true, then 790,000 dollars is a bargain.

505
00:29:43,693 --> 00:29:46,993
You know, you sound just like a real estate agent.

506
00:29:47,063 --> 00:29:48,963
I'm not here to sell a house.

507
00:29:51,993 --> 00:29:52,993
From the looks of you,

508
00:29:53,063 --> 00:29:54,933
she could've ripped you off for a million dollars.

509
00:29:55,563 --> 00:29:57,273
Your wife is going easy on you.

510
00:29:57,473 --> 00:30:00,643
Rip me off? What am I, a Band-Aid?

511
00:30:00,773 --> 00:30:04,713
- Pay up. - Pay up? I can't listen anymore.

512
00:30:05,143 --> 00:30:06,173
Listen here.

513
00:30:06,513 --> 00:30:08,543
I have nothing more to say to someone...

514
00:30:08,613 --> 00:30:10,313
who is so disrespectful.

515
00:30:10,913 --> 00:30:13,083
- Disrespectful? - Yes, disrespectful.

516
00:30:14,353 --> 00:30:17,753
- Abuse, profanity, assault. - What do you think you're doing?

517
00:30:17,823 --> 00:30:19,393
What, you deny it?

518
00:30:20,563 --> 00:30:22,093
Then how about this?

519
00:30:22,563 --> 00:30:24,933
- Refusal of sexual relations. - Hey, give that to me.

520
00:30:25,063 --> 00:30:26,433
Give it to me, now!

521
00:30:29,463 --> 00:30:32,173
Know your enemy and know yourself.

522
00:30:33,333 --> 00:30:36,003
First, you need to understand yourself.

523
00:30:36,873 --> 00:30:39,873
It means admitting that your mess is, in fact, a mess.

524
00:30:39,873 --> 00:30:42,143
That's where the fight begins.

525
00:30:43,213 --> 00:30:44,953
Come back when you're ready for a divorce.

526
00:30:45,013 --> 00:30:46,383
We'll talk then.

527
00:31:09,343 --> 00:31:10,343
But...

528
00:31:10,973 --> 00:31:12,673
please don't cross the line.

529
00:31:13,573 --> 00:31:14,983
The moment you cross that line,

530
00:31:15,083 --> 00:31:16,713
be it in business or anything else,

531
00:31:18,153 --> 00:31:19,783
I won't just stand by.

532
00:31:32,763 --> 00:31:34,603
The model for the finale of this show...

533
00:31:34,863 --> 00:31:36,563
will be Kim Yu Ju.

534
00:31:37,303 --> 00:31:39,773
Ms. Kim is a long time muse...

535
00:31:40,003 --> 00:31:42,943
who provides my husband with design inspiration.

536
00:31:56,483 --> 00:31:57,493
Secretary Han.

537
00:31:58,023 --> 00:31:59,493
Do some digging on Kim Yu Ju for me.

538
00:32:01,463 --> 00:32:03,963
This show really all depends on you, Yu Ju.

539
00:32:04,533 --> 00:32:05,633
If you do well,

540
00:32:05,693 --> 00:32:07,133
you'll save the show and me along with it.

541
00:32:07,533 --> 00:32:10,833
I'm not just saying that. I'm counting on you.

542
00:32:12,273 --> 00:32:13,773
And...

543
00:32:13,843 --> 00:32:16,703
are you and your boyfriend getting along these days?

544
00:32:17,743 --> 00:32:21,113
Oh, you're single. Then I have nothing to worry about.

545
00:32:21,683 --> 00:32:23,083
All right. I'll see you then.

546
00:32:23,613 --> 00:32:24,983
Yes, take care.

547
00:32:25,513 --> 00:32:26,513
Yes.

548
00:32:29,823 --> 00:32:32,493
Hey. Aren't you overdoing it?

549
00:32:32,893 --> 00:32:34,893
The whole show depends on Kim Yu Ju?

550
00:32:35,093 --> 00:32:37,433
Of course I'm overdoing it. But I have to lay it on thick...

551
00:32:37,433 --> 00:32:38,963
so she feels the pressure.

552
00:32:39,463 --> 00:32:42,033
If this show gets ruined because of Yu Ju again,

553
00:32:42,103 --> 00:32:43,873
Baek Mi Young might actually divorce me.

554
00:32:44,533 --> 00:32:47,803
Is this Trunk Show really that important to you?

555
00:32:47,873 --> 00:32:50,543
I'm going to make this show a huge success...

556
00:32:50,613 --> 00:32:52,173
to win Mi Young's heart back...

557
00:32:52,243 --> 00:32:54,383
and completely crush that jerk Calvin.

558
00:32:54,683 --> 00:32:56,543
So he'll never even think of coming near Mi Young again.

559
00:32:57,153 --> 00:32:58,153
But...

560
00:32:58,653 --> 00:33:00,923
I don't think it's going to be that simple.

561
00:33:02,323 --> 00:33:05,093
- What? - I'm talking about Kim Yu Ju.

562
00:33:05,653 --> 00:33:07,863
She already has a history of flaking on a show,

563
00:33:07,963 --> 00:33:10,533
so it's a bit risky to just trust her blindly.

564
00:33:11,193 --> 00:33:13,433
That's true. But what can I do?

565
00:33:15,963 --> 00:33:18,733
Then, should I go pick her up myself?

566
00:33:19,903 --> 00:33:21,343
You're going to pick her up?

567
00:33:21,673 --> 00:33:24,043
The moment Kim Yu Ju wakes up on the day of the show,

568
00:33:24,113 --> 00:33:25,513
I'll pick her up and bring her right over.

569
00:33:26,013 --> 00:33:28,213
Hey, that would work.

570
00:33:28,343 --> 00:33:30,343
That's our Kyung Tae, always thinking.

571
00:33:31,353 --> 00:33:33,283
Hey, hurry up and look at this so we can go get some noodles.

572
00:33:33,453 --> 00:33:34,453
Okay.

573
00:33:34,883 --> 00:33:36,553
Oh, there's a lot of new stuff.

574
00:33:39,023 --> 00:33:40,253
Hello.

575
00:33:40,423 --> 00:33:43,093
- It's been a while. - It's good to see you.

576
00:33:43,223 --> 00:33:44,233
Welcome.

577
00:33:44,533 --> 00:33:46,563
I'm sorry about last year.

578
00:33:46,863 --> 00:33:49,433
I felt terrible after bailing on the show.

579
00:33:49,563 --> 00:33:52,303
You have to keep your promise this time.

580
00:33:52,403 --> 00:33:53,503
Of course.

581
00:33:54,043 --> 00:33:57,243
By the way, CEO Ji was right.

582
00:33:57,873 --> 00:33:59,513
- He was? - When he first called...

583
00:33:59,513 --> 00:34:01,143
to offer me the job,

584
00:34:01,483 --> 00:34:03,643
he said that his wife and I...

585
00:34:03,713 --> 00:34:05,753
have a very similar vibe.

586
00:34:06,453 --> 00:34:08,753
That's why he said he had his eyes on me.

587
00:34:12,223 --> 00:34:13,893
Oh, that's true.

588
00:34:14,193 --> 00:34:16,763
Now that I see you two, she looks just like you did...

589
00:34:16,823 --> 00:34:18,463
when you were younger, CEO Baek.

590
00:34:19,063 --> 00:34:21,233
So, what should I start with?

591
00:34:21,303 --> 00:34:23,303
First, should we get your measurements?

592
00:34:23,363 --> 00:34:24,373
Come this way.

593
00:35:02,443 --> 00:35:04,743
Oh, come on. What is it?

594
00:35:05,143 --> 00:35:06,643
Just wait a second.

595
00:35:07,173 --> 00:35:08,483
Seriously.

596
00:35:11,853 --> 00:35:16,023
- Yes? - Open your eyes when I say three.

597
00:35:16,753 --> 00:35:18,693
Okay. Hurry up.

598
00:35:19,653 --> 00:35:22,263
One, two.

599
00:35:22,363 --> 00:35:23,493
three.

600
00:35:37,003 --> 00:35:38,143
What do you think?

601
00:35:47,723 --> 00:35:49,123
Are you surprised?

602
00:35:51,293 --> 00:35:52,293
Yes.

603
00:35:55,123 --> 00:35:57,633
This is my first piece.

604
00:35:58,293 --> 00:36:00,093
It's still a bit rough, isn't it?

605
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:01,833
No.

606
00:36:02,903 --> 00:36:04,303
It's so beautiful.

607
00:36:07,503 --> 00:36:09,103
Mi Young, then...

608
00:36:11,173 --> 00:36:12,413
will you wear this...

609
00:36:14,083 --> 00:36:15,783
and walk with me?

610
00:36:20,383 --> 00:36:21,523
Will you...

611
00:36:22,853 --> 00:36:24,153
marry me?

612
00:37:13,573 --> 00:37:16,843
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

613
00:37:21,383 --> 00:37:23,543
When he first called to offer me the job,

614
00:37:24,083 --> 00:37:28,223
he said that his wife and I have a very similar vibe.

615
00:37:33,293 --> 00:37:35,263
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

616
00:37:45,473 --> 00:37:46,473
CEO Baek.

617
00:37:50,103 --> 00:37:51,213
What did you think of Kim Yu Ju?

618
00:37:53,543 --> 00:37:56,383
What style do you think suits Kim Yu Ju best?

619
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:58,483
She looked good in pretty much everything.

620
00:37:58,813 --> 00:37:59,953
Probably because she's a good model.

621
00:38:00,853 --> 00:38:02,483
What? You're always so indecisive.

622
00:38:03,623 --> 00:38:04,793
Anyway, discuss it with Director Song...

623
00:38:04,853 --> 00:38:05,853
and give me your feedback.

624
00:38:06,623 --> 00:38:08,863
The finale dress has to be finished by this weekend.

625
00:38:10,363 --> 00:38:11,533
It was because of Calvin.

626
00:38:13,163 --> 00:38:14,163
What?

627
00:38:17,673 --> 00:38:19,173
I pushed for Kim Yu Ju,

628
00:38:20,073 --> 00:38:23,143
not because of you, but because of Calvin.

629
00:38:24,443 --> 00:38:25,943
Because I didn't want to lose to him.

630
00:38:27,843 --> 00:38:28,843
No, but...

631
00:38:29,813 --> 00:38:31,853
why are you telling me this now?

632
00:38:33,713 --> 00:38:35,083
I want this Trunk Show...

633
00:38:36,383 --> 00:38:38,153
to be a success to prove a point.

634
00:38:42,893 --> 00:38:44,463
Separate from our relationship,

635
00:38:45,333 --> 00:38:47,333
J&White, which we built together,

636
00:38:48,133 --> 00:38:49,703
I want to prove myself properly.

637
00:38:50,803 --> 00:38:53,473
Okay, I know what you mean.

638
00:38:54,543 --> 00:38:56,373
I'll finish the dress without any setbacks,

639
00:38:56,443 --> 00:38:57,443
so don't worry.

640
00:38:59,113 --> 00:39:01,843
Let's work together to make this Trunk Show a success.

641
00:39:04,513 --> 00:39:05,553
So, as you can see,

642
00:39:05,613 --> 00:39:08,323
it continues into this off-the-shoulder dress...

643
00:39:08,583 --> 00:39:10,893
We brighten the tone with glamorous jewellery.

644
00:39:16,663 --> 00:39:20,093
And this part is the most important, so please pay close attention.

645
00:39:22,733 --> 00:39:24,203
Okay, just one thing now...

646
00:39:24,273 --> 00:39:26,933
That way, the jewellery can be seen from a distance.

647
00:39:27,173 --> 00:39:28,973
Something new here...

648
00:39:29,243 --> 00:39:30,443
Yes, we'll get started.

649
00:39:43,783 --> 00:39:44,793
This looks good.

650
00:39:45,653 --> 00:39:48,463
Start with the beige one, please.

651
00:39:54,733 --> 00:39:58,733
But how did you come up with that idea?

652
00:39:59,473 --> 00:40:01,473
- What? - The finale dress.

653
00:40:02,403 --> 00:40:04,943
It's an homage to the dress I wore at our wedding.

654
00:40:05,713 --> 00:40:07,913
An homage to the dress you wore at our wedding?

655
00:40:10,113 --> 00:40:11,113
Isn't it?

656
00:40:12,253 --> 00:40:13,253
The sketch...

657
00:40:14,153 --> 00:40:16,423
looked almost identical to my wedding dress.

658
00:40:16,683 --> 00:40:18,893
Oh, that kind of design is common.

659
00:40:18,993 --> 00:40:21,093
It's simple, pure, and has no frills.

660
00:40:23,693 --> 00:40:25,333
Then what about Kim Yu Ju?

661
00:40:25,663 --> 00:40:27,063
Why did you decide to work with Kim Yu Ju again?

662
00:40:27,563 --> 00:40:29,703
She's the one who contacted me first.

663
00:40:30,133 --> 00:40:32,203
She said she was very sorry for the mistake she made last year.

664
00:40:32,503 --> 00:40:34,573
She wanted to make up for it this year or something.

665
00:40:35,243 --> 00:40:37,743
So I gave her a special opportunity.

666
00:40:37,973 --> 00:40:39,513
We even agreed to half her usual fee,

667
00:40:39,573 --> 00:40:41,943
so it all worked out. Good move, right?

668
00:40:47,283 --> 00:40:49,053
Honestly, "personality differences" is a bit much, don't you think?

669
00:40:49,523 --> 00:40:50,523
What?

670
00:40:50,783 --> 00:40:53,423
You wrote "personality differences" in the complaint.

671
00:40:53,953 --> 00:40:55,193
But look at today, for example.

672
00:40:55,263 --> 00:40:56,593
Did we really have anything to fight about?

673
00:40:56,863 --> 00:40:59,593
As long as we don't bring up the divorce, we get along just fine.

674
00:41:00,793 --> 00:41:04,103
Or maybe we're just being peaceful because we're at the Pigeon Market.

675
00:41:04,303 --> 00:41:06,633
You know, since pigeons are a symbol of peace.

676
00:41:12,013 --> 00:41:13,013
You think that's funny?

677
00:41:13,713 --> 00:41:14,713
You don't think it's funny?

678
00:41:17,443 --> 00:41:19,553
This is exactly what I mean by "personality differences."

679
00:41:21,083 --> 00:41:22,953
What about this is suddenly "personality differences"?

680
00:41:23,353 --> 00:41:25,823
I've suddenly lost my appetite.

681
00:41:26,753 --> 00:41:28,093
Ma'am, the check, please.

682
00:41:28,393 --> 00:41:30,223
Hey, where are you going? We're not done eating.

683
00:41:30,793 --> 00:41:31,793
None of your business.

684
00:41:32,663 --> 00:41:33,763
Hey, wait up.

685
00:41:38,173 --> 00:41:40,173
She's like a bomb just waiting to go off.

686
00:41:41,043 --> 00:41:43,673
I have no idea when, where, or how she'll explode.

687
00:41:43,743 --> 00:41:45,273
I tried so hard to be accommodating.

688
00:41:45,343 --> 00:41:47,173
Was that really something to blow up about?

689
00:41:47,413 --> 00:41:48,983
You two are at war right now.

690
00:41:49,513 --> 00:41:50,813
In a war, no one warns you...

691
00:41:50,813 --> 00:41:54,953
three seconds before a bomb goes off, saying, "Watch out."

692
00:41:55,353 --> 00:41:57,553
You just have to accept reality.

693
00:41:57,693 --> 00:42:00,553
But did I start this war?

694
00:42:00,753 --> 00:42:02,163
She filed the complaint whenever she felt like it,

695
00:42:02,263 --> 00:42:04,393
and now she attacks me over every little thing I say.

696
00:42:05,463 --> 00:42:07,633
But she has no problem smiling at some other guy.

697
00:42:07,963 --> 00:42:09,333
What other guy?

698
00:42:09,663 --> 00:42:11,033
There's this one jerk.

699
00:42:11,633 --> 00:42:15,403
So she smiles at this jerk,

700
00:42:16,543 --> 00:42:17,873
but she's out for your blood?

701
00:42:18,113 --> 00:42:20,043
Yes, she's out for my blood.

702
00:42:20,113 --> 00:42:21,543
And I don't even know what I did wrong.

703
00:42:25,583 --> 00:42:26,583
I can't let this go.

704
00:42:27,483 --> 00:42:29,423
I need to get to the bottom of this.

705
00:42:30,153 --> 00:42:31,153
Won Ho.

706
00:42:31,453 --> 00:42:32,453
Won Ho.

707
00:42:41,533 --> 00:42:43,963
We're like oil and water.

708
00:42:45,903 --> 00:42:48,243
Just when I think I'm starting to soften up,

709
00:42:49,143 --> 00:42:50,743
we'll say a few words to each other,

710
00:42:51,243 --> 00:42:53,143
and before I know it, we're at each other's throats.

711
00:42:53,673 --> 00:42:55,713
The two of you are on such different wavelengths...

712
00:42:56,383 --> 00:42:57,713
that it's brought you to this point.

713
00:42:58,553 --> 00:42:59,553
Exactly.

714
00:43:00,083 --> 00:43:01,953
That's why I skipped trying for an uncontested divorce...

715
00:43:02,623 --> 00:43:04,153
and went straight for the lawsuit.

716
00:43:04,353 --> 00:43:05,753
I knew we'd never be able to agree on anything.

717
00:43:06,453 --> 00:43:09,993
Were you guys unable to communicate...

718
00:43:10,793 --> 00:43:11,963
that it led to what happened that day?

719
00:43:13,433 --> 00:43:14,463
That day?

720
00:43:15,233 --> 00:43:16,233
That day.

721
00:43:16,763 --> 00:43:19,973
The day of your suicide attempt.

722
00:43:28,343 --> 00:43:29,343
Don't come any closer.

723
00:43:29,613 --> 00:43:30,843
Mi Young, just put that down.

724
00:43:31,183 --> 00:43:32,913
- Don't come any closer. - Put it down.

725
00:43:36,153 --> 00:43:37,283
I said let go.

726
00:43:39,293 --> 00:43:40,823
Please, ma'am.

727
00:43:40,893 --> 00:43:43,563
- Mom, we have guests inside. - And what does that matter?

728
00:43:43,623 --> 00:43:45,133
I'm what's most important. Out of my way. Move.

729
00:43:45,193 --> 00:43:46,193
No, ma'am, please.

730
00:43:46,263 --> 00:43:47,903
That's enough. Come out. I said that's enough.

731
00:43:47,933 --> 00:43:49,603
Where is she? Come out.

732
00:43:49,663 --> 00:43:50,663
Ma'am, please, just a moment.

733
00:43:50,733 --> 00:43:52,033
- Ma'am, she's... - Where is she?

734
00:43:52,303 --> 00:43:53,303
Oh, dear.

735
00:43:53,903 --> 00:43:54,903
Mother.

736
00:43:56,673 --> 00:43:58,313
She's my mother-in-law.

737
00:43:59,043 --> 00:44:02,883
- Ma'am, please calm down. - Mom.

738
00:44:02,943 --> 00:44:04,043
I said let go.

739
00:44:04,883 --> 00:44:06,083
I'm so sorry, Mi Young.

740
00:44:06,183 --> 00:44:07,513
I tried my best to stop her.

741
00:44:08,083 --> 00:44:11,223
Are you really going to go through with a lawsuit against Won Ho?

742
00:44:12,723 --> 00:44:15,093
Answer me. Yes or no?

743
00:44:16,193 --> 00:44:17,193
So it's true?

744
00:44:19,793 --> 00:44:21,703
Ma'am, please, have a seat...

745
00:44:21,763 --> 00:44:22,763
You stay out of this.

746
00:44:24,003 --> 00:44:25,733
Is what you wrote in the complaint really true?

747
00:44:27,003 --> 00:44:29,603
I'm asking if you really meant what you wrote.

748
00:44:33,413 --> 00:44:34,413
Tell me.

749
00:44:35,383 --> 00:44:37,853
What was your real reason for filing the complaint?

750
00:44:38,783 --> 00:44:39,783
That would be me.

751
00:44:41,083 --> 00:44:42,953
I'm the one who sent the complaint.

752
00:44:43,453 --> 00:44:44,453
And who are you?

753
00:44:44,793 --> 00:44:46,823
I'm Baek Mi Young's divorce attorney,

754
00:44:48,363 --> 00:44:49,393
Jeon Chi Hyun.

755
00:44:51,023 --> 00:44:52,033
So you're the one?

756
00:44:52,293 --> 00:44:53,893
You're the one who spouted all that nonsense?

757
00:44:54,163 --> 00:44:56,133
If you have an objection to the contents of the complaint,

758
00:44:56,303 --> 00:44:57,933
please prepare a formal response and submit it.

759
00:44:58,003 --> 00:45:00,003
There's no need to trouble yourself by coming here in person.

760
00:45:00,403 --> 00:45:01,403
What?

761
00:45:02,173 --> 00:45:03,573
A consultation will be difficult today.

762
00:45:04,303 --> 00:45:05,343
I'll come back another time.

763
00:45:06,073 --> 00:45:08,083
Hey. Get back here!

764
00:45:09,183 --> 00:45:10,313
- Mom. - That woman...

765
00:45:10,383 --> 00:45:11,383
What are you doing?

766
00:45:14,053 --> 00:45:16,053
- Ma'am, please stop! - Mom!

767
00:45:19,153 --> 00:45:20,993
You've got some nerve.

768
00:45:21,793 --> 00:45:23,263
Mom.

769
00:45:24,933 --> 00:45:26,933
- Mom, stop. - Let go!

770
00:45:27,563 --> 00:45:28,963
- Mi Young. - Mom.

771
00:45:30,133 --> 00:45:31,173
Who do you think you are?

772
00:45:31,873 --> 00:45:33,733
- What do you know about it? - No, you can't.

773
00:45:33,803 --> 00:45:35,273
- What do you know? - Ma'am.

774
00:45:35,343 --> 00:45:36,573
What do you know?

775
00:45:41,443 --> 00:45:42,443
Mom.

776
00:45:44,983 --> 00:45:46,383
Let go of her hair. Mom.

777
00:45:48,253 --> 00:45:51,623
- Ma'am, please, let her go. - So what if you're a lawyer?

778
00:45:53,893 --> 00:45:56,123
- Ma'am, please let go. - Let go. Let her go, Mom.

779
00:45:56,193 --> 00:45:57,393
What? What was that?

780
00:46:17,213 --> 00:46:18,213
Who do you think you are?

781
00:46:21,783 --> 00:46:24,823
Mi Young, you're making me a birthday dinner yourself?

782
00:46:25,093 --> 00:46:27,423
It's nothing fancy, but I brought a few things.

783
00:46:27,653 --> 00:46:29,693
Mi Young, let me help you cook...

784
00:46:30,863 --> 00:46:32,863
What are you thinking, with your bad back?

785
00:46:33,063 --> 00:46:36,263
Don't. You need to be in good shape to have a baby.

786
00:46:36,763 --> 00:46:39,273
A man can have children until the day he dies.

787
00:46:39,873 --> 00:46:40,873
But a woman...

788
00:46:42,243 --> 00:46:43,443
You know what I mean, right?

789
00:46:44,343 --> 00:46:46,073
Mi Young, did you tell Won Ho...

790
00:46:46,243 --> 00:46:48,183
that you can't get pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

791
00:46:48,513 --> 00:46:50,183
- What? - Why would he say...

792
00:46:50,183 --> 00:46:51,813
something like that if you didn't?

793
00:46:53,883 --> 00:46:55,453
I think I'm finally starting to understand.

794
00:46:57,453 --> 00:46:59,653
After I received the complaint, I felt so wronged the whole time.

795
00:47:01,863 --> 00:47:03,563
I kept wondering why this was happening to me.

796
00:47:05,093 --> 00:47:06,963
What could I have possibly done so wrong?

797
00:47:10,803 --> 00:47:12,103
But when I actually...

798
00:47:13,333 --> 00:47:14,943
saw it with my own eyes,

799
00:47:16,703 --> 00:47:18,443
it all became clear in an instant.

800
00:47:23,013 --> 00:47:25,053
If that's the reality of marriage,

801
00:47:27,383 --> 00:47:29,923
then maybe divorce is the answer.

802
00:47:35,963 --> 00:47:36,963
So?

803
00:47:40,763 --> 00:47:41,963
I'm just going to accept it.

804
00:47:44,203 --> 00:47:45,233
The mess I made...

805
00:47:48,643 --> 00:47:49,743
is, in fact, a mess.

806
00:47:52,013 --> 00:47:53,413
You've come a long way.

807
00:47:54,913 --> 00:47:57,543
So I'm going to give her what she wants, as much as I can.

808
00:47:59,113 --> 00:48:01,523
I'll give my wife everything she wants,

809
00:48:03,323 --> 00:48:05,593
and end things cleanly.

810
00:48:08,463 --> 00:48:09,563
Are you sure you won't regret this?

811
00:48:11,493 --> 00:48:12,493
Yes.

812
00:48:13,233 --> 00:48:14,233
I won't regret it.

813
00:48:14,563 --> 00:48:15,563
Really?

814
00:48:20,573 --> 00:48:21,573
All right.

815
00:48:22,143 --> 00:48:23,173
Good.

816
00:48:24,473 --> 00:48:26,143
Then let's move forward.

817
00:48:43,216 --> 00:48:46,356
Are you really going to go through with a lawsuit against Won Ho?

818
00:48:47,233 --> 00:48:49,403
Answer me. Yes or no?

819
00:48:50,263 --> 00:48:51,263
Are you happy?

820
00:48:53,233 --> 00:48:54,233
Are you?

821
00:48:58,443 --> 00:48:59,443
Are you...

822
00:49:01,273 --> 00:49:02,443
living a good life?

823
00:49:04,013 --> 00:49:05,013
We're like...

824
00:49:05,513 --> 00:49:07,053
oil and water.

825
00:49:08,783 --> 00:49:11,123
Just when I think I'm starting to soften up,

826
00:49:11,993 --> 00:49:13,753
we'll say a few words to each other,

827
00:49:14,123 --> 00:49:16,093
and before I know it, we're at each other's throats.

828
00:49:16,823 --> 00:49:18,893
The two of you are on such different wavelengths...

829
00:49:19,533 --> 00:49:20,893
that it's brought you to this point.

830
00:49:21,733 --> 00:49:24,663
Even if all my dreams came true right now,

831
00:49:25,673 --> 00:49:28,503
I'm sure I'd just develop a new longing.

832
00:49:30,303 --> 00:49:32,343
I want to go further,

833
00:49:32,813 --> 00:49:35,013
all the way to the finish line.

834
00:49:36,543 --> 00:49:37,913
I want this trunk show...

835
00:49:39,053 --> 00:49:40,883
to be a success to prove a point.

836
00:49:41,923 --> 00:49:43,483
Separate from our relationship,

837
00:49:44,383 --> 00:49:46,453
J&White, which we built together,

838
00:49:47,193 --> 00:49:48,893
I want to prove myself properly.

839
00:50:22,923 --> 00:50:23,923
Today...

840
00:50:27,833 --> 00:50:30,563
Mi Young, we'll go wait in the car.

841
00:50:39,973 --> 00:50:40,973
What brings you here?

842
00:50:41,743 --> 00:50:42,883
I came to show my support.

843
00:50:43,913 --> 00:50:44,913
To wish you luck on the show today.

844
00:50:47,383 --> 00:50:48,383
I'll do my best.

845
00:50:49,083 --> 00:50:50,083
Is that all?

846
00:50:51,023 --> 00:50:52,423
If there's anything I can do to help,

847
00:50:52,493 --> 00:50:53,553
just say the word, Mi Young.

848
00:50:54,553 --> 00:50:55,923
All you have to do is ask,

849
00:50:57,123 --> 00:50:58,463
and I can solve anything for you.

850
00:50:59,493 --> 00:51:01,363
You're as confident as ever.

851
00:51:02,503 --> 00:51:03,703
I'm sorry, Calvin.

852
00:51:04,563 --> 00:51:06,603
But I'd rather work hard and fail on my own...

853
00:51:06,873 --> 00:51:08,973
than have you solve my problems for me.

854
00:51:10,173 --> 00:51:11,243
So...

855
00:51:11,673 --> 00:51:13,143
please, don't cross the line.

856
00:51:14,413 --> 00:51:16,113
And don't just show up unannounced like this.

857
00:51:26,323 --> 00:51:27,653
- Over here, please. - Here?

858
00:51:27,723 --> 00:51:30,223
- Look this way, please. - Yes, great.

859
00:51:30,563 --> 00:51:31,563
Yes.

860
00:51:40,533 --> 00:51:42,473
- Good morning, Bruni. - Good morning.

861
00:51:42,573 --> 00:51:44,443
Everything okay?

862
00:51:44,643 --> 00:51:45,643
Yes.

863
00:51:59,523 --> 00:52:00,523
Mr. Ji?

864
00:52:07,063 --> 00:52:08,663
You look really great today.

865
00:52:08,863 --> 00:52:10,003
Oh, what's all this?

866
00:52:10,803 --> 00:52:12,173
What are you doing here?

867
00:52:12,573 --> 00:52:15,643
I'm here for work. I work for the Calvin Hotel now.

868
00:52:15,903 --> 00:52:17,643
I'm here to take pictures for today's show.

869
00:52:23,743 --> 00:52:25,353
I didn't get a chance to say this last time...

870
00:52:25,413 --> 00:52:26,553
because things were so chaotic.

871
00:52:28,183 --> 00:52:30,023
Don't. You don't have a chance.

872
00:52:31,023 --> 00:52:33,523
- Excuse me? - Don't like me.

873
00:52:35,623 --> 00:52:36,663
By any chance,

874
00:52:37,123 --> 00:52:38,733
is there someone you like?

875
00:52:39,963 --> 00:52:40,963
What?

876
00:52:42,663 --> 00:52:43,663
CEO Ji.

877
00:52:44,403 --> 00:52:45,603
Oh, yes, I'm coming.

878
00:52:46,873 --> 00:52:49,073
Anyway, I've made myself clear.

879
00:52:54,143 --> 00:52:55,143
You're here early.

880
00:52:57,043 --> 00:52:58,043
Great atmosphere, right?

881
00:53:16,763 --> 00:53:18,733
Yes, check them one by one with a long ruler.

882
00:53:18,803 --> 00:53:19,803
Yes, got it.

883
00:53:19,873 --> 00:53:21,103
Please hurry.

884
00:53:22,473 --> 00:53:24,373
Excuse me, coming through. Sorry, excuse me.

885
00:53:25,643 --> 00:53:26,943
These aren't the right earrings.

886
00:53:27,713 --> 00:53:28,713
Just a moment.

887
00:53:30,613 --> 00:53:31,783
Yes, Vice President Kang,

888
00:53:31,983 --> 00:53:34,353
you're picking up Kim Yu Ju and are on your way now, right?

889
00:53:35,123 --> 00:53:37,683
Yes, CEO Baek. I've just arrived.

890
00:53:38,823 --> 00:53:39,823
Yes.

891
00:53:39,953 --> 00:53:42,223
If there's no traffic, I think we'll get there a bit early.

892
00:53:44,823 --> 00:53:45,833
What?

893
00:53:46,163 --> 00:53:47,163
Room 301?

894
00:53:48,163 --> 00:53:49,603
CEO Baek, just a moment.

895
00:53:50,763 --> 00:53:53,103
Mr. Kang?

896
00:53:56,143 --> 00:53:57,143
Yu Ju.

897
00:53:58,103 --> 00:53:59,113
Yu Ju?

898
00:53:59,843 --> 00:54:00,843
Are you in there?

899
00:54:02,113 --> 00:54:03,113
Yu Ju.

900
00:54:06,283 --> 00:54:07,283
Yu Ju.

901
00:54:09,783 --> 00:54:10,783
Yu Ju.

902
00:54:12,353 --> 00:54:13,353
Yu Ju.

903
00:54:13,553 --> 00:54:15,763
Are you okay? Yu Ju.

904
00:54:17,563 --> 00:54:19,593
Yu Ju, please wake up.

905
00:54:20,263 --> 00:54:21,263
Yu Ju.

906
00:54:21,493 --> 00:54:22,533
Yu Ju.

907
00:54:31,043 --> 00:54:33,043
I'm really looking forward to today's show.

908
00:54:34,243 --> 00:54:35,313
Me too.

909
00:54:35,383 --> 00:54:36,913
It's truly an honour to be collaborating with you.

910
00:54:37,383 --> 00:54:39,483
Oh, your Italian is quite fluent.

911
00:54:39,653 --> 00:54:41,723
Yes, I studied in Milan for a short time.

912
00:54:41,923 --> 00:54:42,923
Milan?

913
00:54:43,583 --> 00:54:45,793
I see. What a nice surprise.

914
00:54:45,893 --> 00:54:46,893
Thank you.

915
00:54:53,693 --> 00:54:57,363
What? The finale model isn't here yet?

916
00:54:58,163 --> 00:54:59,403
What's going on?

917
00:55:07,213 --> 00:55:08,443
How could this happen?

918
00:55:09,443 --> 00:55:11,243
So, what are Yu Ju's injuries exactly?

919
00:55:11,313 --> 00:55:12,383
How badly is she hurt?

920
00:55:12,583 --> 00:55:13,713
Vice President Kang is with Yu Ju now.

921
00:55:13,783 --> 00:55:16,253
He called an ambulance and is on the way to the hospital with her.

922
00:55:16,783 --> 00:55:19,593
He said it looks like her leg is broken.

923
00:55:21,393 --> 00:55:22,423
What do we do?

924
00:55:22,663 --> 00:55:26,263
Thank goodness the vice president found her when he did.

925
00:55:26,633 --> 00:55:28,093
She'll be fine once she gets treatment.

926
00:55:29,263 --> 00:55:32,073
Right. Yu Ju will be fine.

927
00:55:32,503 --> 00:55:33,633
What about our show?

928
00:55:34,633 --> 00:55:36,643
What do you mean Yu Ju isn't here yet?

929
00:55:36,743 --> 00:55:38,813
Yu Ju got hurt, so she can't make it.

930
00:55:39,343 --> 00:55:41,143
She's on her way to the hospital with the vice president now.

931
00:55:42,313 --> 00:55:43,313
Darn it.

932
00:55:43,983 --> 00:55:44,983
Then...

933
00:55:45,253 --> 00:55:47,883
who's going to walk in the finale?

934
00:55:49,323 --> 00:55:50,583
We'll have to get someone else.

935
00:55:50,653 --> 00:55:51,923
We can't just stand here and do nothing.

936
00:55:52,793 --> 00:55:55,493
Director Song, you have that list of available models, right?

937
00:55:55,963 --> 00:55:56,963
Yes.

938
00:55:56,963 --> 00:55:59,263
Let's call every single model on that list.

939
00:56:00,033 --> 00:56:02,503
We'll be able to find one model who can walk the finale.

940
00:56:03,363 --> 00:56:04,403
I'm counting on you.

941
00:56:04,703 --> 00:56:05,773
Yes, got it.

942
00:56:16,043 --> 00:56:17,613
If we find a new finale model,

943
00:56:17,843 --> 00:56:19,613
we'll alter the dress and put her in it immediately,

944
00:56:19,883 --> 00:56:21,283
so stay on your toes.

945
00:56:21,653 --> 00:56:23,823
But what if we can't find a model for the finale...

946
00:56:23,883 --> 00:56:24,923
That won't happen.

947
00:56:25,523 --> 00:56:27,723
I will make this Trunk Show a success.

948
00:56:28,493 --> 00:56:29,723
Okay.

949
00:56:33,263 --> 00:56:34,263
Sir.

950
00:56:34,393 --> 00:56:36,303
It seems they haven't found a finale model yet.

951
00:56:39,833 --> 00:56:42,943
The show is about to start, and if they still haven't found one,

952
00:56:43,643 --> 00:56:45,313
it's safe to say the finale is in jeopardy, right?

953
00:56:45,643 --> 00:56:46,643
What should we do?

954
00:56:46,943 --> 00:56:49,513
- We could hire one of our models... - Let's...

955
00:56:49,683 --> 00:56:50,683
just watch.

956
00:56:52,283 --> 00:56:55,053
Let's not cross the line. We'll wait for now.

957
00:56:55,653 --> 00:56:56,783
Yes, sir.

958
00:57:02,723 --> 00:57:04,523
She's on an overseas shoot?

959
00:57:05,533 --> 00:57:06,963
Yes, I see. Nothing we can do, then.

960
00:57:07,763 --> 00:57:08,763
Yes.

961
00:57:09,303 --> 00:57:11,333
What are we going to do?

962
00:57:11,763 --> 00:57:13,403
Has no one said yes yet?

963
00:57:13,773 --> 00:57:14,773
No.

964
00:57:14,833 --> 00:57:17,403
Of all times, it's during Fashion Week.

965
00:57:18,303 --> 00:57:20,543
Doesn't anyone know someone they can call?

966
00:57:24,283 --> 00:57:27,353
What do we do? The show's about to start.

967
00:57:27,783 --> 00:57:29,383
What's the plan, CEO Baek?

968
00:57:33,723 --> 00:57:37,223
We will now begin the Trunk Show for Bruni & Co. and J&White.

969
00:58:06,893 --> 00:58:08,093
Who did they say is doing the finale?

970
00:58:08,323 --> 00:58:10,893
I heard they haven't found anyone yet.

971
00:58:10,993 --> 00:58:12,733
This is a complete disaster.

972
00:58:22,503 --> 00:58:25,203
The finale is in ten minutes.

973
00:58:27,913 --> 00:58:29,283
We're so screwed.

974
00:58:29,743 --> 00:58:31,843
Where did the two CEOs go?

975
00:58:34,583 --> 00:58:35,823
Good question.

976
00:58:37,153 --> 00:58:39,923
Are they off crying in a corner somewhere?

977
00:58:40,453 --> 00:58:41,453
No.

978
00:58:42,593 --> 00:58:44,263
The finale is in ten minutes.

979
00:58:44,323 --> 00:58:45,793
I know. So why are we here?

980
00:58:46,093 --> 00:58:48,263
Ji Won Ho, you can do an alteration right now, can't you?

981
00:58:48,563 --> 00:58:49,863
An alteration? Here?

982
00:58:50,063 --> 00:58:51,063
What are you talking about?

983
00:58:51,803 --> 00:58:53,673
The finale is going on as planned.

984
00:58:53,833 --> 00:58:55,273
How? We don't have a model.

985
00:58:56,343 --> 00:58:57,343
I'm doing it.

986
00:58:57,603 --> 00:58:58,603
What?

987
00:59:03,513 --> 00:59:05,753
Ji Won Ho, I'm giving you ten minutes.

988
00:59:30,943 --> 00:59:32,173
And now for tonight's highlight.

989
00:59:32,513 --> 00:59:34,443
Our finale model makes her entrance.

990
01:00:26,133 --> 01:00:28,093
(Special Thanks to Lee Su Ji for Her Guest Appearance)

991
01:00:40,673 --> 01:00:43,613
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

992
01:00:45,243 --> 01:00:48,183
I don't see why not. Let's do it. The collaboration.

993
01:00:48,513 --> 01:00:51,723
- What? - Don't ruin this. Get on board.

994
01:00:51,783 --> 01:00:53,653
What do you mean, "get on board?"

995
01:00:53,723 --> 01:00:58,323
- What, am I your puppy? - Like the calm before the storm.

996
01:00:58,393 --> 01:01:00,033
Why Calvin got divorced...

997
01:01:00,393 --> 01:01:02,263
I came because I have something to give you in person.

998
01:01:02,433 --> 01:01:05,703
The vibe between them was definitely different than usual.

999
01:01:06,333 --> 01:01:07,333
And if I don't stay put?

1000
01:01:07,403 --> 01:01:08,503
Then I'll have to do something more.

1001
01:01:10,003 --> 01:01:11,543
Revenge?

